# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and the
# corpus out of the image. `node_modules` and `.git` are the obvious two, but
# the third is the one that actually matters here:

# .env is gitignored, and a Dockerfile COPY does not care about .gitignore.
# Without this line the real .env — with whatever key is in it — is copied into
# a layer, where it survives even a later `rm` and can be read out of the image
# history by anyone who can pull it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The corpus is committed to git but MUST still be kept out of the image. It is
# 17 MB today and grows with the corpus, and a PDF baked into a layer stays in the
# image history even if the bind mount later shadows it. The mount is one line
# and makes the PDFs swappable without a rebuild, which is the point.
data/pdfs/*
!data/pdfs/.gitkeep

# The scanned-PDF copy at the repo root. PDF_DIR points at data/pdfs, so the
# ingest path never sees this one.
listofproducts.pdf

# Prepared index snapshots. Bind-mounted at runtime for the same reason the PDFs
# are: one is ~20 MB today and grows with the corpus, and a snapshot baked into a
# layer stays in the image even after the mount shadows it. It is also a derived
# artifact — regenerable with `npm run index:export` — so it does not belong in
# an image at all.
index-snapshots

# Not ignored on purpose: test/. The suite runs with no devDependencies, so
# keeping it means `docker compose run --rm app npm test` works in the image
# with nothing extra installed.
node_modules
.git
.gitignore
*.log
.DS_Store
doc
